 "planning_findings_for_plan_integrator": [
  {
   "id": "TE4-F1",
   "target": "specialists/slice-graph.md S12 row",
   "finding": "S12 is the only phase assembly slice without CMD-SECRETS and CMD-RULES, yet PROC-ASSEMBLY runs both at the last step and the phase repair verification (DEC-GM-038) requires them.",
   "proposed_text": "S12 Proposed commands: \"PROC-ASSEMBLY, CMD-TEST-ALL, CMD-SMOKE, CMD-SECRETS, CMD-RULES\""
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F2",
   "target": "specialists/slice-graph.md S46 row",
   "finding": "AC-GM-LANE-02 requires the compose smoke after each merge and the final repair verification requires CMD-SMOKE, but S46 lists no CMD-SMOKE; docs are served by the app at /llms.txt, /guide.md, /kit/.",
   "proposed_text": "S46 Proposed commands: \"PROC-ASSEMBLY, CMD-TEST-ALL, CMD-SMOKE, CMD-SECRETS, CMD-RULES\""
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F3",
   "target": "specialists/slice-graph.md S17 row",
   "finding": "S17 edits deploy/Dockerfile and deploy/compose.yaml but runs no smoke, so a broken image reaches S18 unseen.",
   "proposed_text": "S17 Proposed commands: \"CMD-RED-GREEN, CMD-TEST-PARITY, CMD-BENCH, CMD-DEPSCAN, CMD-SMOKE, CMD-WRITESET\" and append to the S17 goal: \"make depscan RUST=1; make smoke SMOKE_PROJECT=gm-smoke-rust SMOKE_PORT=18002.\""
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F4",
   "target": "specialists/slice-graph.md S01 goal (and design.md DES-GM-ARCH if it names the mutmut config)",
   "finding": "Per-phase lean mutation (DEC-GM-038) needs every phase core module in the mutmut config; the S01 goal names market.py only. The bots container runs the bots.py stub from S08 on, and CMD-SMOKE requires it to stay running. Dashboard tests need Testing Library and jsdom. Subprocess backends (MCP tests, smoke) need a database path that is not the container default.",
   "proposed_text": "In the S01 goal replace `backend/pyproject.toml [tool.mutmut] paths_to_mutate = [\"gridmarket_server/market.py\"]` with `backend/pyproject.toml [tool.mutmut] paths_to_mutate = [\"gridmarket_server/market.py\", \"gridmarket_server/economy.py\", \"gridmarket_server/decision_router.py\", \"gridmarket_server/health.py\", \"gridmarket_server/adversary.py\"] and tests_dir = [\"tests/\"]`; and append: \"bots.py stub whose __main__ idles in a sleep loop until the bots lane replaces it; dashboard devDependencies vitest, @testing-library/react and jsdom with vitest environment jsdom in vite.config.ts (admission scan); main.py reads the SQLite path from GRIDMARKET_DB (default /data/gridmarket.db), listed in CONTRACTS.md and .env.example; Makefile test-mcp exits 1 with MCP_PROJECT_ABSENT until mcp-server/pyproject.toml exists.\""
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F5",
   "target": "design.md DES-GM-OPS (compose.yaml bots service)",
   "finding": "The bots service needs GRIDMARKET_BOT_SECRET from the env file; DES-GM-OPS gives the GM_ENV_FILE env_file entry to `app` only, so CMD-SMOKE's throwaway env file would not reach the bots container and it would crash or read ../.env.",
   "proposed_text": "In DES-GM-OPS replace \"`bots` (same image, command `python -m gridmarket_server.bots`)\" with \"`bots` (same image, command `python -m gridmarket_server.bots`, the same `env_file` entry `{path: ${GM_ENV_FILE:-../.env}, required: false}`, `read_only: true`, `restart: unless-stopped`)\""
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F6",
   "target": "specialists/slice-graph.md S09, S49, S12, S46 goals",
   "finding": "The goals tell the Integration Engineer to \"run\" the AC-GM-ACC-03/01/02 acceptance runs and the AC-GM-DOC-02 guide demonstration, but those are owner-run (credential access: owner env file, tunnel) or Orchestrator-dispatched (clean agent session) procedures with no actor and in no slice command_ids.",
   "proposed_text": "S09: replace \"run the AC-GM-ACC-03 acceptance run\" with \"hand the phase 1a candidate to the owner for PROC-ACCEPT-P1A (owner-run, Scribe-recorded)\"; S49: replace \"run AC-GM-ACC-01\" with \"hand the candidate to the owner for PROC-ACCEPT-P1 (AC-GM-ACC-01)\"; S12: replace \"run the AC-GM-ACC-02 acceptance run incl. the simulated LoneStar outage\" with \"hand the candidate to the owner for PROC-ACCEPT-P2 (AC-GM-ACC-02, incl. the simulated LoneStar outage)\"; S46: replace \"run the AC-GM-DOC-02 guide demonstration with a clean agent session and a sandbox key\" with \"hand the candidate to the Orchestrator for PROC-GUIDE-DEMO (AC-GM-DOC-02)\"."
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F7",
   "target": "gridmarket-technical-plan.md RISK-GM-07 (Requirements Engineer)",
   "finding": "PROC-ACCEPT-P1 and PROC-ACCEPT-P2 (AC-GM-ACC-01, AC-GM-ACC-02) run through the tunnel on Saturday, but RISK-GM-07 and RISK-GM-14 say the tunnel is open only from the recording through Sun 15:00 CDT.",
   "proposed_text": "RISK-GM-07 mitigation: replace \"tunnel open only from recording through 15:00 CDT Sunday\" with \"tunnel open only during the owner's acceptance runs and from the recording through 15:00 CDT Sunday\"; same change in RISK-GM-14."
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F8",
   "target": "implementation.json (Plan Integrator)",
   "finding": "Phase cadence needs per-phase assurance commands with no slice owner; owner and Orchestrator procedures must stay out of slice command_ids.",
   "proposed_text": "Copy seit.json phase_assurance into implementation.json as the per-phase assurance block (required commands, MUTANTS selection, coverage base, smoke project and port, red-then-green pairs, acceptance procedure, repair_verification_commands). PROC-LANDING, PROC-ACCEPT-P1A, PROC-ACCEPT-P1, PROC-ACCEPT-P2, PROC-GUIDE-DEMO, PROC-ERCOT-LIVE-CHECK, PROC-TUNNEL and PROC-ADV-DEMO carry no actor and appear in no slice command_ids."
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F9",
   "target": "journey.json (Orchestrator)",
   "finding": "CELL-GM-DISCLAIMER-PLACEMENT is DEFERRED in journey.json but resolved by Planning (README Contributors S45 + lane receipts); CELL-GM-KICKOFF-DECK still BLOCKED although a63c8d2 transcribed the deck (TE-F7 carried).",
   "proposed_text": "Orchestrator records CELL-GM-DISCLAIMER-PLACEMENT as resolved by Planning with that placement and re-checks CELL-GM-KICKOFF-DECK; decision_baseline is then reprojected without row changes."
  },
  {
   "id": "TE4-F10",
   "target": "specialists/slice-graph.md S38 goal",
   "finding": "S38 writes mcp-server/tests/ before S39 creates the mcp-server project, so the red run must use the backend environment and import gridmarket_mcp inside each test, or it fails in collection (RED_GREEN_UNBOUND).",
   "proposed_text": "Append to the S38 goal: \"Import gridmarket_mcp inside each test or fixture; red run with make red-green SUITE=mcp (backend environment); mcp-server/tests/conftest.py blocks outbound sockets except 127.0.0.1 and starts the backend with GRIDMARKET_DB on a temporary path.\""
  },
  {
   "id": "PD-RECON-1",
   "target": "seit.json PROC-ACCEPT-P1, SEIT-GM-ACC-01/02 rows",
   "finding": "Planning and Design reconciliation after RE gate r3: AC-GM-ACC-01 and AC-GM-ACC-02 now run against the integrated candidate, not through the tunnel, which also resolves TE4-F7 without changing RISK-GM-07 or RISK-GM-14.",
   "proposed_text": "applied by Planning and Design"
  }
 ],
